        Under <strong>Full Jitter</strong>, the sleep duration is drawn from a uniform continuous distribution:
      </p>
      <div class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-300 overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <code>t ~ U(0, min(cap, base * 2^attempt))</code>
      </div>
      <p>
        Because the probability density function is uniform across the entire interval from zero to the exponential ceiling, workers that failed at identical moments are distributed smoothly along the entire time horizon. The probability of two independent workers selecting the identical millisecond window approaches zero as attempt count grows.
      </p>

